{#
    Analytics' tabs, as links: what has happened (`/stats`) and what is about
    to (`/forecast`).

    Analytics is one rail item over two screens, and these are what make the
    second one findable — the model is the Settings page's tabs. Each is a
    page of its own, so each works without script and can be bookmarked, and
    the rail lights Analytics on both. `aria-current="page"` marks the one
    shown, and the underline is drawn from it.

    `tab`  'overview' or 'forecast'
#}
<nav class="page-tabs" aria-label="{{ t('stats.tabs_label') }}">
    <ul class="page-tabs-list">
        <li>
            <a href="/stats" {{ tab == 'overview' ? 'aria-current="page"' : '' }}>{{ t('stats.tab_overview') }}</a>
        </li>
        <li>
            <a href="/forecast" {{ tab == 'forecast' ? 'aria-current="page"' : '' }}>{{ t('stats.tab_forecast') }}</a>
        </li>
    </ul>
</nav>
